1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,293
The second attempt began with a plan on a plastic desk under a low ceiling.

2
00:00:04,293 --> 00:00:14,467
The committee had asked them to perform one investigation before they spent another month: could the tool be built without the equipment they did not have?

3
00:00:14,467 --> 00:00:24,231
“You must realize,” the landlord said, “that the smoke alarm is the only thing in this building that always works.”

4
00:00:24,231 --> 00:00:34,145
The advantage of the small team was its availability: a photographer, a lecturer, a retailer, and a chemist were all free that week.

5
00:00:34,145 --> 00:00:44,274
Together they could construct a demo on a desktop in three days, and they could buy the spare parts from a second hand vendor in the cave of a market.

6
00:00:44,274 --> 00:00:52,023
“The face of the customer is the only specification that means anything,” Maya said.

7
00:00:52,023 --> 00:00:58,323
It would be a promising performer, this tool, if they could keep it honest.

8
00:00:58,323 --> 00:01:05,577
“A composer, a robot, and an opera singer all use the same punch card,” she said.

9
00:01:05,577 --> 00:01:17,491
“The difference is what they do with the sound.” They would spend the week on the quantification of something that could not be counted, and they would do it together.

10
00:01:17,491 --> 00:01:22,201
The competitive pressure was speculative and therefore endless.

11
00:01:22,201 --> 00:01:33,799
A coupon in a cancelled buffet, a fry cook's opener, and the notional promise of a hack from a rival firm: all of it had to be folded into the plan.

12
00:01:33,799 --> 00:01:44,453
“You could say the software would evolve,” Lin wrote, “but evolution is not fiction, and cancellation is not a strategy.”

13
00:01:44,453 --> 00:01:48,253
The industrious part was the tireless part.

14
00:01:48,253 --> 00:01:54,523
Today they counted what the tool did; tomorrow they would count what it failed to do.

15
00:01:54,523 --> 00:01:58,312
“The month is not the unit,” she said.

16
00:01:58,312 --> 00:02:06,812
“The failure is.” It was a mean way to put it, and it was also the only way that would keep them honest.

17
00:02:06,812 --> 00:02:14,751
The police had asked whether the tool would be available to everyone, and the answer was not yet available either.

18
00:02:14,751 --> 00:02:31,209
A small parade of questions followed: could a second hand vendor sell it, would the committee buy the plan, must they spend the month on the demonstration, and would they, together, be able to face the small print?

19
00:02:31,209 --> 00:02:37,007
They would, they said, and today they meant it.
